  "proof": [
    "IntoMap changes only the lower Map definitions and its output cache. It never mutates the lower input or descendant nodes.",
    "If the upper Map disappears, the changed lower Map is replacement depth0. If the upper Map remains, a fresh upper Map is depth0 and changed lower Map depth1.",
    "Depth1 therefore covers all changes and their child-first output refresh. Root output equality, owning worklist, exclusions, and mandatory conservative final pass remain unchanged.",
    "Current depth2 safely over-approximates those mutations, but when the upper Map disappears it reaches every child of a wide unchanged UnionAll below the lower Map. These unchanged sources are refreshed and requeued unnecessarily.",
    "When the upper Map remains, depth2 additionally refreshes/requeues the unchanged lower input. The amendment omits that work.",
    "ThroughInput retains depth2: its kept upper Map, modified input, and new child Maps can occupy replacement depths0,1,2."
  ],
